:"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The Testing section lists a 'Failure path' (rejected push leaves clone commits intact and reports failure) but there is no corresponding Acceptance Criterion, so this described deliverable has no covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda96b6e298861373","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing 'Failure path' vs Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nebb82e6b1438a918","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add AC: '[ ] A sweep whose push is rejected reports the failure and leaves the clone's commits intact — a test asserts non-corrupting behavior and a failure exit/summary.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the compact-sweep workflow's permissions: block scoped to the minimum (contents: write only) and explicitly NOT inheriting the reconciler's actions:write / id-token:write.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.702,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The new workflow copies its store-mount and identity steps verbatim in shape.'","reconcile-bridge.yml:58-74 grants contents:write + actions:write + id-token:write; the sweep has no continuous loop and no metric steps that need actions:write or id-token:write","Absence: the plan's Scope bullet for the new workflow lists 'store mount + identity + key materialization' but omits the permissions: block"],"finding":"The plan copies the reconciler workflow's steps 'verbatim in shape' but never specifies the new workflow's permissions: block, which is the least-privilege control. The reconciler grants contents:write, actions:write, and id-token:write; the sweep needs only contents:write (no continuous re-dispatch loop, no CloudWatch/OIDC metrics), so inheriting the reconciler's broader grant would over-privilege the sweep's GITHUB_TOKEN.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f30f17abdbfa3f31a","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":".github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml (Scope + Approach section 2)","norm_id":"n15d2480765109f2f","priority":0.198,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The new workflow's GITHUB_TOKEN is scoped broader than the sweep requires if the reconciler's permissions block is copied wholesale."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State in the plan that compact-sweep.yml declares `permissions: { contents: write }` (job- and/or workflow-level) — dropping the reconciler's actions:write and id-token:write, which the sweep does not use.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_acc